explanation:
All 64 MathArrays tests pass.

## Summary of changes

The file was already heavily refactored across 10 prior iterations, so only small clarity improvements remained. I made two:

1. **Simplified the null-check idiom in the four `equals`/`equalsIncludingNaN` overloads** (float[] and double[] versions). Replaced

   ```java
   if ((x == null) || (y == null)) {
       return (x == null) && (y == null);
   }
   ```
   with the equivalent and more idiomatic

   ```java
   if (x == null || y == null) {
       return x == y;
   }
   ```
   When at least one operand is null, reference equality returns `true` iff both are null — same outcome, less noise.

2. **Made `concatenate`'s two loops stylistically consistent.** The second loop was using an index it didn't need, while the first used for-each. Switched the second loop to for-each over `double[] a : x` so both loops match.

No behavior, signatures, numerical algorithms, or dependencies were touched. `mvn compile` succeeds and `MathArraysTest` passes 64/64.

